      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix Mooncake Store decode-save offset stalls when SWA blocks have been evicted locally but their keys already exist remotely.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Count remotely existing keys as saved, even when their local sources are unavailable.\n- Keep the checkpoint incomplete when a key is missing remotely and has no usable local source.\n- Exclude unavailable sources from value preparation and PUT.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe new regression fails before the fix (`assert 1 == 2`: the evicted block's key was excluded from the existence query) and passes afterward. Four existing parametrized cases retain coverage for remotely missing keys with unavailable sources.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_store_worker.py -q\n```\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Worker unit suite | 249 passed |\n| Seven related Mooncake test files | 369 passed |\n| Ruff, relevant mypy, whitespace checks | Passed |\n\n**A/B:** \nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017, 8 H20 GPUs, TP=8, Mooncake Store `kv_both`, decode saves enabled, eager MRV2, block size 64. A 513-token seed prompt generates one token, followed by a 514-token prompt generating 768 tokens.\n\n| Observation | Baseline | PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Generated tokens | 768 | 768 |\n| Decode-save checkpoint | Blocked by evicted local sources despite existing remote keys | Completed using remote existence checks |\n| Saved offset across all 8 ranks | Remained at 0 | Advanced on every rank |\n\nCounts cover parseable shared-stdout records; some lines interleaved. A separate cleanup-equivalence A/B using per-process JSONL confirmed 104/104 completed decode saves and final offset 1280 on every rank in both arms.\n\nReal-model validation was performed locally. Full pre-commit setup timed out installing an unrelated hook; relevant hooks passed separately.\n\n## Details\n\nPreviously, the sender skipped NULL/out-of-range sources before `batch_is_exist()` and unconditionally marked the checkpoint incomplete. SWA eviction therefore blocked offset advancement even for already-persisted keys.\n\nThe sender now builds all relevant keys, checks remote existence, and filters PUTs by local source availability.\n\n| Remote key | Local source | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Exists | Any | Satisfied; no PUT |\n| Missing | Available | PUT; require success |\n| Missing | Unavailable | Do not advance offset |\n\nThis is a small connector-local change with no new synchronization. It adds existence checks for relevant keys previously skipped.\n\nDuplicate check on 2026-11-01 found no equivalent fix. Related PRs #63511, #55097, and #62400 address async-MTP save frontiers, direct P/D alignment, and lookup boundaries respectively.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Small connector-local fix using existing functionality.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Local regression and real-model validation passed; Buildkite selection and source dependencies still need confirmation.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Focused diff; relevant static checks passed.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes root cause, related work, validation, and limitations.\n</details>\n\n",
